---
title: Asynchronous acceptance and accounting retry
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as Sandbox platform
    participant I as Go ingress
    participant K as Kafka streams
    participant W as Go accounting worker
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over P,D: Row selector: customer_billing_state.customer_id = C

    P->>I: Submit usage with stable source and event IDs
    I->>K: Publish raw events with durable replication settings
    K-->>I: Replicated acceptance
    I-->>P: Accepted. accounting may still be pending
    Note over P: Producer buffer can mark these events as delivered.<br/>Acceptance does not imply a fresh credit balance.
    Note over K,W: Aggregation prepares replay-safe identified deltas.<br/>The raw archive has an independent consumer group.

    K->>W: Deliver an identified accounting delta
    W->>D: BEGIN and lock FOR UPDATE<br/>customer_billing_state.customer_id = C
    W->>D: Check delta identity. apply financial effect if new
    W->>D: Save processed ID and state outbox record
    W->>D: COMMIT financial effect and processed identity
    D-->>W: Durable commit
    Note over W: Worker crashes before its offset is committed.

    K->>W: Redeliver the same delta to a restarted worker
    W->>D: Customer transaction: check the processed identity
    D-->>W: Already accounted. no additional credit debit
    W->>D: End transaction without a new financial effect
    W->>K: Commit the processed offset
    K-->>W: Offset recorded

    Note over K,D: Kafka and PostgreSQL do not share this transaction.<br/>Stable identities make replay financially idempotent.
    %% This sequence shows option D. Option C uses a PostgreSQL inbox instead of Kafka.
